101
00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.717
Yeah. never get between
that man and a fish.

102
00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:07.870
Sir. I got your son
on video chat.

103
00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.234
Excellent.

104
00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.794
He had his first date
last night.

105
00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.792
Mr. President.
you need to take this. sir.

106
00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.393
Sir.
Speaker of the House?

107
00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.878
You need to
take this now. sir.

108
00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.193
This is the President.

109
00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.674
Okay. Thank you.

110
00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.593
<i>Sources confirmed</i>

111
00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.989
<i>that Prime Minister
James Wilson has died</i>

112
00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.038
<i>while sleeping in his residence
at 10 Downing Street.</i>

113
00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.116
<i>He is believed to have
suffered a heart attack.</i>

114
00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.590
<i>possibly from complications
after a surgical procedure</i>

115
00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.830
<i>to repair his knee
a day earlier.</i>

116
00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:00.753
<i>An autopsy has been scheduled
within the next 48 hours</i>

117
00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.637
<i>to determine
the actual cause of death.</i>

118
00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:03.720
It's the White House.

119
00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.078
It's okay.
My mom can come over.

120
00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.120
What we are proposing

121
00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.077
is that the funeral takes
place this Thursday. the 9th.

122
00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.912
4:00 p.m.
at St. Paul's.

123
00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.032
The confirmed attendees
are all world leaders.

124
00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.680
with the lone exception
of the Russian president.

125
00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:43.352
Well.
no love lost there.

126
00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:46.717
Our Royal Family will
attend a private service

127
00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:48.631
at St. James's Palace.
the morning of.

128
00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:52.633
with 28 other heads of state
from all over the globe.

129
00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:56.315
As per foreign royals.
Prince Albert of Monaco.

130
00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.789
Queen Rania of Jordan.
Saudi Prince Muqrin.

131
00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.871
Yes. it's a
logistical nightmare.

132
00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.752
But let's make sure
this runs without a hitch.

133
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.115
Questions?

134
00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:10.914
And what special requests have
the Yank circus demanded so far?

135
00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.998
Dallas Cowboy cheerleaders
part of the retinue. possibly?

136
00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:16.355
That's a
request I could live with.

137
00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.831
I'm partial to the Kardashians myself.
as apparently is Her Majesty.

138
00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.958
Nineteen special requests
from 12 different countries.

139
00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.071
We've denied all of them.

140
00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.959
Any issues of special concern
with our current assessments?

141
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.600
We all know about the 350
or so British nationals

142
00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:37.000
who've traveled back and forth
to Syria in the past year.

143
00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:40.633
as we've seen before
in Iraq and Afghanistan.

144
00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.348
Of rising concern
is the handful

145
00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:45.793
we believe to be
former military.

146
00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:47.199
Is any of this
actionable?

147
00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:48.838
No.

148
00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.154
Very well.

149
00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.476
Then we will see off our dear
friend James with dignity.

150
00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.236
Give him the ceremony
he deserves.

151
00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:04.959
Sir?

152
00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.319
Are you ready for us?
Oh.

153
00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:07.719
Yeah. come on in.

154
00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.034
Take a seat.

155
00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.956
What are you guys
so damn nervous about?

156
00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:23.119
The Brits are world class.
We all know their reputation.

157
00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.794
But still. these are
the trips I hate.

158
00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:29.236
Last minute. Out of the country.
No time to plan.

159
00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.436
Are you sure I can't
talk you out of this?

160
00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:34.834
Lynne.
it's a state funeral.

161
00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:36.911
It's our oldest.
strongest ally.

162
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.151
I spent half the night on the
line with our advance team.

163
00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:43.352
Metropolitan Police will secure
the perimeter of the funeral

164
00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:44.555
at St. Paul's Cathedral.

165
00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.035
Air Force One will land
at Stansted Airport.

166
00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.752
On the ground
it's all Mike.

167
00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:53.994
Touchdown. Then a 12-minute
chopper ride to Somerset House.

168
00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.469
From there we take
an armored-vehicle escort

169
00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:59.916
down Fleet Street
to the cathedral.

170
00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.193
You don't
seem thrilled.

171
00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.197
Well. the British
have their hands full.

172
00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:08.477
It's a clusterfuck...
Sir.

173
00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.637
Well. 40
different countries

174
00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.392
with 40 different
security teams.

175
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.070
Minimal flexibility
on approach routes.

176
00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.549
funeral seating. egress.

177
00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.029
Can we make it work?

178
00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.189
Mike?

179
00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.588
I always do. sir.

180
00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:26.920
Good.

181
00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.434
I know it's not great
timing for you. but...

182
00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.519
It's what I do.

183
00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:33.919
Thank you. sir.

184
00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.195
There's my man.

185
00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.511
Mr. Vice President.
How was your vacation. sir?

186
00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:58.515
Son. do you have any idea
the joy a man feels

187
00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.397
pulling
a 70-pound king mackerel

188
00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.198
out of the waters
around Jekyll Island?

189
00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.594
No. sir. I don't.

190
00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:04.908
That makes two of us.

191
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.400
And I'll have to wait
until next year to find out.

192
00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:10.030
But thanks for asking.

193
00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.032
Oh. yeah.
that's in the Sinai.

194
00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:26.157
- It's beautiful.
- There you go.

195
00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:28.800
Oh. gee. that's incredible.
I love these things. They all are...

196
00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.069
Don't worry about a thing.
We'll be fine.

197
00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:38.919
Doris.
can we have a minute?

198
00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:40.473
Sure.

199
00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.473
Oh. you meant Leah.
Right.

200
00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:45.675
Very funny. Doris.

201
00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.830
And she tells me
not to worry.

202
00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.633
It's only three days.

203
00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.635
Yeah. And I'm not
due for two weeks.

204
00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:03.034
The walking away ain't
quite so easy this time.

205
00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:06.994
Hey. I got this.

206
00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.310
You go and you do
what you have to do

207
00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:14.150
and we will be right here
when you get back. okay?

208
00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.232
You. say bye-bye
to Daddy.

209
00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:18.960
Hmm.

210
00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.072
Bye-bye. Daddy.

211
00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.350
Bell tolls.

212
00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.480
Yeah.

213
00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.511
I love you.

214
00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:37.432
You better.

215
00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.238
Behave.

216
00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.149
Uh. here you go.
Thank you.

217
00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:10.517
You've been hiding lately.
You busy nesting?

218
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:12.670
Something like that.
Mmm-hmm.

219
00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:16.469
Your idea of nesting being bullet-proofing
the walls of the nursery?

220
00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:18.875
Now. that is actually a great idea.

221
00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.719
Yes.

222
00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:28.639
I'll do it.

223
00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:34.150
Well...
That only took two weeks.

224
00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:37.915
Uh-uh. It's no small
thing being a godmother.

225
00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.594
I mean. I didn't take
your asking lightly.

226
00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:43.309
Oh. I know.

227
00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:45.436
You think
you can handle it?

228
00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:47.840
Well. I'm competent. brilliant.

229
00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:50.354
stunningly beautiful and
really fucking honored.

230
00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:54.239
Really honored.

231
00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:56.280
Thank you. Lynne.

232
00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.554
Big day ahead.

233
00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.113
Correction. Mega day.

234
00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:18.753
Morning.

235
00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:21.075
Thank you.

236
00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:26.748
Just your signature here. please.
Thank you. sir.

237
00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.799
Gentlemen. ladies.

238
00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:36.554
Today. I need
your undivided best.

239
00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:39.837
The most important people in
the world are in our care.

240
00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:42.798
so muck in
and get it right.

241
00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:44.480
Always. Chief. Hmm.

242
00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.469
Good morning. London.

243
00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.511
Southpaw
has landed.

244
00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:18.435
Agent Banning.
John Lancaster from 5.

245
00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.192
Hey. John.
Bit early. aren't you?

246
00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.350
Nope.
We're moving up our schedule.

247
00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:23.708
I see.

248
00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:26.832
The fewer people know the President's
exact movements. the better.

249
00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.319
Why wasn't I told?

250
00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.719
Nobody was.

251
00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:31.518
That's how
you keep it a surprise.

252
00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:33.793
Well.
thanks for the help.

253
00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.236
<i>With security at unprecedented levels</i>

254
00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:45.276
<i>in anticipation
